<title>USA: Timken reaches 3-year agreement with union.</title>
<headline>Timken reaches 3-year agreement with union.</headline>
<dateline>CANTON, Ohio 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Timken Co said it and the United Steelworkers of America, AFL-CIO, agreed on a new three-year labor contract.</p>
<p>Timken said in a statement that members of the USW voted Tuesday and Wednesday to ratify a new contract, which takes effect in September 1997 when the current contract expires.</p>
<p>Certain provisions become effective sooner, the company said.</p>
<p>The new contract extends through September 24, 2000, the company added.</p>
<p>Officials at the company were not immediately available to comment further.</p>
</text>
